SCORP SYSTEM PORTAL - LEGACY FIRMWARE ENVIRONMENT CHARTER
=========================================================

This custom project architecture, front-end routing framework, user interface layout, 
and deployment file package designed for the PlayStation 4 homebrew environment 
(specifically optimized for systems running firmware versions 5.05 through 13.00), 
is the exclusive intellectual property of Ahmed Essam (GitHub: scorpion511).

SECTION I: DEPLOYMENT STIPULATIONS & IDENTITY PROTECTIONS

1. INTERFACE RECOGNITION & ATTRIBUTION
   The visual framework design, neon typography style layout, menu sorting rules, and 
   branding elements known as "SCORP HOST" are uniquely authored and compiled by Ahmed Essam. 
   Any public server deployments, mirror sites, or community forks tracking this software 
   package must preserve prominent and visible attribution strings ("Designed By Ahmed Essam") 
   on the interface layout at all times.

2. CLONING RESTRICTIONS & NAME REPACKAGING
   No external party, individual, or developer is authorized to strip this repository of its 
   rightful ownership text, replace the creator's signatures with their own name, or attach 
   a conflicting license file wrapper onto unauthorized duplicates of this file package tree. 
   Doing so constitutes a violation of copyright and instantly revokes all permissions to host 
   or mirror these structural layouts.

3. CONSOLE RESOURCE WRAPPING
   This master interface serves as a visual wrapper that initializes independent community 
   exploitation scripts, payload injection binaries (such as GoldHEN suites), and kernel 
   offset arrays required to complete system verification procedures. These background payload 
   files and core execution routines maintain their respective independent homebrew community roots 
   and are not claimed under the copyright of this front-end presentation wrapper.

SECTION II: RISK MANAGEMENT CLAUSES

1. EXCLUSION OF LIABILITY
   THIS INTERFACE HUB IS DISTRIBUTED FOR PRIVATE EVALUATION PURPOSES ON AN "AS IS" BASIS. 
   THE AUTHOR ASSEPTS ABSOLUTELY ZERO LIABILITY OR WARRANTY FOR DATA INSTABILITY, SYSTEM 
   UNRESPONSIVENESS, INTERNAL STORAGE FREEZES, OR FIRMWARE CORRUPTION THAT MAY OCCUR ON 
   YOUR RELEVANT SYSTEM ENVIRONMENT DURING EXPLOIT OPERATION PROCEDURES.
